<section class="philosophy section">
  <div class="container philosophy-inner">
    <div class="philosophy-text">
      <p>
        In Sanskrit, Setu (सेतु) means bridge —<br />
        connecting two shores without disturbing either.
      </p>
      <p>
        GitSetu bridges the gap between the developer you are<br />
        in one directory and the developer you are in another.<br />
        Invisibly. Correctly. Without asking anything of you<br />
        after the first setup.
      </p>
      <p class="philosophy-highlight">
        A tool that demands your attention has failed.<br />
        GitSetu succeeds when you forget it exists.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .philosophy {
    background: var(--bg-secondary);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
  }

  .philosophy-inner {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .philosophy-text {
    max-width: 800px;
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  .philosophy-text p {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .philosophy-text p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .philosophy-highlight {
    color: var(--text-heading);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: var(--text-2xl);
    position: relative;
    display: inline-block;
  }

  .philosophy-highlight::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    bottom: -8px;
    left: 10%;
    width: 80%;
    height: 2px;
    background: var(--gradient-accent);
    opacity: 0.5;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .philosophy-text {
      font-size: var(--text-lg);
    }
    
    .philosophy-highlight {
      font-size: var(--text-xl);
    }
  }
</style>
